# team-hub-web

## Purpose
- Angular frontend for Team Hub.

## Scope
- Authentication, profile, organizations management UI, invitations, and notifications inbox.
- Uses gateway-backed API paths and GraphQL BFF for selected composed reads.

## Runtime and ports
- Local dev app: Angular dev server (standard project scripts).
- Dev API proxy: `/api` -> `https://localhost:8080` (infrastructure nginx).
- Docker/runtime: frontend exposed on `https://localhost:4200` (`ui-web`).

## API integration
- Auth API base: `/api/auth/v1`.
- Organization API base: `/api/organizations/v1`.
- Notification API base: `/api/notifications/v1`.
- Chat API base: `/api/chat/v1` (reserved/integration-ready).
- GraphQL BFF: `/api/graphql`.

## Runtime flow
- Browser -> `ui-web` -> nginx/gateway path `/api/...` -> backend services.
- Frontend does not call backend services directly by container URL.

## Security and request context
- Uses JWT bearer for protected calls.
- Sends `X-Correlation-ID` and `X-Session-ID` via HTTP interceptors.
- Uses `withCredentials` where auth/session flow requires cookies.

## Configuration
- Environment files: `src/environments/environment.ts`.
- Dev proxy config: `proxy.conf.json`.
- Main app code: `src/app/**`.

